ve_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- v4.6.rc2.official [78c6632eb]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc2 - macOS Sequoia (15.7.3) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the FileSystem dock is **at the bottom** and set into _horizontal split_ view mode, the two areas of the dock (folders at the top and the contents of the selected folder at the bottom) are really hard to see. They blend together a lot. This is most apparent in a brand new project, since there are no files to indicate that these are two separate panels. It looks like a really big gap.\n\n<img width=\"906\" height=\"468\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1156364-1a71-475a-8d00-2b88714f0cbb\" />\n\nWith the filesystem dock at the side this is not an issue, since it's visually divided by the _Filter Files_ field. This is also the case in earlier versions (4.5.1) - the filter field visually divides the two areas. Just for reference:\n\n<img width=\"417\" height=\"699\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c95eb7c5-2e3f-46b2-8d50-6934775afd5f\" />\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nPerhaps the two areas could be separated with underlying panels - it's the case with _vertical split_. It looks good.\n\n<img width=\"921\" height=\"468\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ab18cd1d-bb33-48db-bf41-8f97d2d75ddd\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new godot project\n- Move file dock to the bottom slot\n- Switch file dock into the _horizontal split_ mode\n- The `res://` folder and the built-in `icon.svg` have a really big gap in between. Or so it seems!\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nTrivial","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115191/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115191/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}